A||||7||Tweek||Drain holes for sunroof||||1||
Z||000000||Tweek||06-22-2001||04:17 AM||||The oem sunroof on my 84 doesn't usually leak, unless it rains real hard, then it just pours in. Though Im going to look into some new screws with the gaskets, I suspect that it is because of the lack of drain holes for the early years. Im planning on drilling the holes outlined here: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/010923.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/010923.html</A> <P>Does this seem to be the right thing to do??  Would you do it? When it does leak, from the inside the channels along the edge just fill with water, then when they are too full, or I accel. or decell., It drip everywhere.<P>Thanks in advance for any advice you have, even if its to say go for it (which Im hoping to hear)<P>Ted||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tweek||06-22-2001||04:22 AM||||Also, should I drill just rear, front or both? <P>ciao<p>[This message has been edited by Tweek (edited 06-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||06-22-2001||09:19 AM||||Front and rear under the corners of the gasket   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>But if you replace the gasket there should be no need to drill the holes.<p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-22-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||rogergarrison||06-22-2001||10:34 AM||||I dont know if you should just drill holes. Ive never had the roof off mine, but most factory sunroofs with the drains have hoses connected to channel the water down the pillars. If you just drill a hole, you may have water pouring in all kinds of places. Maybe someone familiar with Fiero roofs know how the water exits before you drill.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodrv6||06-22-2001||12:29 PM||||Go ahead and drill the holes.  Just make sure you drill only through the fiberglass upper roof and not into the steel inner roof.  All the Fieros have drain channels built into the steel inner roofs, so the water will drain correctly.  I checked my 84 when I had the body panels off a couple of years ago.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000005||84Bill||06-22-2001||12:39 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>I dont know if you should just drill holes. Ive never had the roof off mine, but most factory sunroofs with the drains have hoses connected to channel the water down the pillars. If you just drill a hole, you may have water pouring in all kinds of places. Maybe someone familiar with Fiero roofs know how the water exits before you drill.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you look at the pictures I provided you can just see a thin gasket about 1/4 inch wide running around the perimeter of the subroof. This keeps the water from dripping in unwanted places<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/op/image014e.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-22-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000006||cadaver||06-22-2001||09:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>I dont know if you should just drill holes. Ive never had the roof off mine, but most factory sunroofs with the drains have hoses connected to channel the water down the pillars. If you just drill a hole, you may have water pouring in all kinds of places. Maybe someone familiar with Fiero roofs know how the water exits before you drill.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Other cars yes but fiero's dont have drain tubes. I think you dont know what you speak of.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Brucepts||06-22-2001||10:14 PM||||I drilled the holes (four of them) one in each corner the other weekend haven't had any water inside since then and mine was as bad as yours!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Advanced Dealer in the Great Material Continuum . . .<BR>Non Fiero Website: <A HREF="http://tractorsport.com" TARGET=_blank>http://tractorsport.com</A> <BR>You can't race a dyno . . .||||reg||1
